    "problem_statement": "# Server crashes when handling disconnected protocols\n\n## Description\n\nI'm experiencing an issue with the server crashing when handling disconnected protocols. The application checker seems to be trying to access an undefined variable.\n\nWhen a client disconnects, the server throws the following error:\n\n```\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/path/to/daphne/server.py\", line 307, in application_checker\n    if not application_instance and disconnected:\nNameError: name 'application_instance' is not defined\n```\n\nThis happens during the application_checker routine that's supposed to clean up disconnected protocols.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start a Daphne server with a simple ASGI application\n2. Connect a client (either HTTP or WebSocket)\n3. Have the client disconnect abruptly\n4. Wait for the application_checker to run (it runs every 1 second)\n\nThe server will crash with the NameError shown above.\n\nThis issue seems to affect both HTTP and WebSocket connections that disconnect. The server is unable to properly clean up disconnected protocols because it's trying to reference a variable that doesn't exist in that scope."
  }
